      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:2:4:4",
      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) وَ أَنَا حَاضِرٌ عَنِ الْمَرْأَةِ تَرَى الصُّفْرَةَ فَقَالَ مَا كَانَ قَبْلَ الْحَيْضِ فَهُوَ مِنَ الْحَيْضِ وَ مَا كَانَ بَعْدَ الْحَيْضِ فَلَيْسَ مِنْهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Al Qasim Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Abu Hamza who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> was asked and I was present, about the woman who sees the yellowness. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Whatever was before the menstruation (<span class=\"iTxt\">Haydh</span>), so it is from the menstruation (<span class=\"iTxt\">Haydh</span>), and whatever was after the menstruation (<span class=\"iTxt\">Haydh</span>), so it is not from it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Khalid from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn abu Hamzah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, was asked, when I was in his presence, about the case of a woman who experiences a discharge of yellowish color. He (the Imam) said, ‘What is before Hayd (menses) is of Hayd (menses) and what is after Hayd (menses) is not Hayd (menses).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
